From 5fa63d53b03fc8b4943f26e9459e9d749f608624 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ore Adeleye <oreadeleye67@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:44:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(er): keep markdown formatting on attribute types that use
 generics

erBox escapes `<` and `>` around createText and restores them afterwards by
assigning `textContent` on the rendered label's first child and each first
descendant. Assigning `textContent` replaces all child nodes, so the
<strong>/<em> elements or styled tspans that markdown produced were thrown
away and the type came out unstyled, e.g. `**List~int~**`.

Only rewrite the text nodes instead, and cover it with a unit test.

